Dealing with Demogorgon without using Elbereth is tricky, but doable.
Moving to the up stairs is definitely a vital part of it, unless you
have stoning grenades or a rubber chicken immediately to hand.

For the purpose of killing Demogorgon, wielded cockatrice eggs are better
than wielded cockatrice corpses, since they don't bring the risk of a
succubus getting you harder than she intended or you wanted.

Wielded potion of paralysis + ring of free action = paralysed Demogorgon
(for 1d25 turns) and still-freely-moving player.  Paralysed Demogorgon =
easily slain Demogorgon, since the player never misses.  Sadly, you can't
accelerate the process of killing Demogorgon with a potion of sickness,
since he is doubly immune to them. (Once for being poison resistant like
all demons, and once for having a deathly-sickness attack.)

Carrying a scroll of scare monster is (once) as good as engraving
Elbereth.

A high-level magic missile while there's a wall behind him can blow off
a huge chunk of his hit points in one casting.  Especially if you've
got reflection or if there's a wall behind *you* as well.
